61
00:15:07,008 --> 00:15:08,768
And there are infinitely many of them.

62
00:15:09,687 --> 00:15:12,048
So A1, A2, A3, A4, A5.

63
00:15:12,148 --> 00:15:13,187
It goes like that.

64
00:15:13,427 --> 00:15:14,128
It never ends.

65
00:15:15,067 --> 00:15:19,408
So you see there are infinitely many numbers listed in order.

66
00:15:20,307 --> 00:15:27,847
So these, so for example, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, dot, dot, dot.

67
00:15:28,587 --> 00:15:29,327
2 times N.

68
00:15:29,427 --> 00:15:33,567
All even numbers, even positive integers listed in this order.

69
00:15:34,067 --> 00:15:35,888
So that's a sequence of numbers.

70
00:15:36,668 --> 00:15:40,967
So these numbers, each of these numbers are called the terms of the sequence.

71
00:15:40,967 --> 00:15:45,367
And so for example, in this sequence, A1 is 2.

72
00:15:46,067 --> 00:15:48,567
A1 is 2 means the first term is 2.

73
00:15:48,707 --> 00:15:50,207
First term of the sequence is 2.

74
00:15:50,668 --> 00:15:51,567
A2 is 4.

75
00:15:52,008 --> 00:15:53,908
So the second term of the sequence is 4.

76
00:15:54,048 --> 00:15:55,008
A3 is 6.

77
00:15:55,127 --> 00:15:56,668
The third term of the sequence is 6.

78
00:15:56,748 --> 00:15:57,207
And so on.

79
00:15:58,668 --> 00:16:01,327
In general, AN is called the nth term.

80
00:16:01,327 --> 00:16:04,687
